==English==

===Etymology===
{{der|en|la|minuendus||something to be diminished}}, gerundive of {{m|la|minuō|decrease, diminish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmɪnjʊˌɛnd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|arithmetic}} A number or quantity from which another is to be subtracted.
#: ''In the subtraction 10 &minus; 4, 10 is the minuend and 4 is the subtrahend.''

